  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 19,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.091,
            0.539,
            0.12
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What you have learnt"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.133,
            0.894,
            0.167
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Carbon is a versatile element that forms the basis for all living organisms and many of the things we use.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.17,
            0.894,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This large variety of compounds is formed by carbon because of its tetravalency and the property of catenation that it exhibits.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.206,
            0.893,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Covalent bonds are formed by the sharing of electrons between two atoms so that both can achieve a completely filled outermost shell.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.241,
            0.892,
            0.276
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Carbon forms covalent bonds with itself and other elements such as hydrogen, oxygen, sulphur, nitrogen and chlorine.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.278,
            0.894,
            0.327
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Carbon also forms compounds containing double and triple bonds between carbon atoms. These carbon chains may be in the form of straight chains, branched chains or rings.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.329,
            0.894,
            0.364
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The ability of carbon to form chains gives rise to a homologous series of compounds "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "in which the same functional group is attached to carbon chains of different lengths.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.365,
            0.893,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The functional groups such as alcohols, aldehydes, ketones and carboxylic acids "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "bestow characteristic properties to the carbon compounds that contain them.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.401,
            0.774,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Carbon and its compounds are some of our major sources of fuels.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.421,
            0.892,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ethanol and ethanoic acid are carbon compounds of importance in our daily lives.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.441,
            0.894,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The action of soaps and detergents is based on the presence of both hydrophobic "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "and hydrophilic groups in the molecule and this helps to emulsify the oily dirt and hence its removal.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.447,
            0.97,
            0.552,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
